3 PAGE Edward Savage Obit
3 DATA
4 DATE 16 Feb 1928
4 TEXT Edward Savage, Veteran, Dies
5 CONT 
5 CONT (1928)
5 CONT 
5 CONT (special to the times)
5 CONT 
5 CONT Chaumont, Feb 7- Edward Savage, 84 died at his home in the town of Hounsfied early Monday morning.
5 CONT 
5 CONT Mr. Savage was born May 26, 1843 in the town of Brownville where he lived until he was two years of age. He then moved into the town of Hounsfield with his parents. He remained there for the remainder of his life with the exception of three years s
5 CONC pent in the army during the Civil war. He was a member of Company H, 10th New York Artiliery,. He lived for seven years in Jersey City, N.J.
5 CONT 
5 CONT He was honary member of Brownville Masonic Lodge No. 53 F. and A.M., a member of Watertown Grange and of the GAR post of Dexter.
5 CONT 
5 CONT Surviving are the following children: May D. Savage and Edward G. Savage who lived home, John Savage of Muscalong, Mrs. Grace J. Wallace of Brownville, George W. Savage of Minneapolis, Minn., Mrs. Emma M. Brooks of East Rodman, Mrs. Eva B. Elliso
5 CONC n [Allison] of Limmerick, Arthur E. Savage of Rochester and nine grandchildren. His wife, Emma Mary Savage, died on Sept 28, 1927.
5 CONT 
5 CONT Funeral Services will be held Thursday at 2pm from the home with interment in Brownville.
5 CONT 
5 CONT Card of thanks
5 CONT 
5 CONT We wish to than the Sons of Veterans, Masons, The Watertown Grange, also our friends and neighbors for their kind expressions of sypathy and floral offerings, especially the use of cars in the sad loss of our beloved father, Edward Savage.
5 CONT 
5 CONT John Savage
5 CONT Edward G. Savage
5 CONT George W. Savage
5 CONT Arthur E. Savage
5 CONT Grace J. Wallace
5 CONT Emma Brooks
5 CONT May D., Ferguson
5 CONT Eva B. Allison
5 CONT 
5 CONT Hounsfield, NY Feb 16, 1928
