1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;Jan (Jacob) Derckse Amerman worked as a sailor for the Dutch West Ind
2 CONC ies Company. He married in 1648 Trinjntie Claes, who lived in Marken in Amsterdam. They were married in Ter Burght (Den Burg on Texel). Marken was the name of an Amsterdam quarter, but also the name of the tiny island in the Zuiderzee. Ter Burght i
2 CONC s probably the town of Den Burg on the island of Texel. Jan and Trinjntie probably set sail together, out of the Port of Texel, the large island off North Holland, the springboard for all Dutch marine adventures about 1649. Most of the ships saile
2 CONC d to England before sailing to the New World. (It is assumed that she may have set sail with her husband at that time).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif
2 CONC ; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; fo
2 CONC nt-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;In 1649 Trinjtie Claes and Jan Jacobse Amerman/Amberman had a son Dierck Janse Amerman/Amberman. Jan, Trinjntie and Dierck Janse Amerman liv
2 CONC ed at Mannadens, section C, which is present-day Manhatten Island, New York. See the Castello Plan 1660.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px
2 CONC ; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'sourc
2 CONC e sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;.............&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px
2 CONC ; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'sourc
2 CONC e sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;"Descendants Of Derick Janse Amerman"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, san
2 CONC s-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #363
2 CONC 22d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;(Dirck Janssen Ammerman) compiled by: C. Theodore Ammerman&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-fam
2 CONC ily: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;50
2 CONC 9 Ivanell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro'
2 CONC , helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;La Puente, CA 91744&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; bac
2 CONC kground-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source san
2 CONC s pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;Pg. 4...The earliest known ancestor of this family line was Jan Dirckee Amerman (1), who is believed to have been a sailor, sailing out of Holland. It is not know
2 CONC n whether he sailed to New Amsterdam, (later New York), or whom his wife was, or how his infant son, Derick Janse Amerman, came to America in the year 1650.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source san
2 CONC s pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&g
2 CONC t;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;Note 1..Letter to this compiler dated 19 Dec., 1968, from Richard H. Amerman, Editor of the Half Moon, p
2 CONC uslished by the Holland Society of New York, quoted as follows: "Origins of our family name are still unclear; some of us think it is of Frisian inception, from "Amersma"; others that it connects in some way with the North Holland town of Amnersfoo
2 CONC rt. Some years ago while in Amsterdam, I got a copy of the marriage banns in 1648 of the couple whose son, Dirck Janse A., came as an infant to this country two years afterward. Dirck lived until about 1723. His father, according to the Amsterdam r
2 CONC ecord (assuming it relates, as I think it does), from the island of Maarken in the Zuyder Zee, was by occupation a sailor. This man's name was Jan Dirckse A., so the patronymic tie-in is clear. A.ll this I relate from recollection, but I believe i
2 CONC t correct."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-f
2 CONC amily: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;Th
2 CONC e name Ammerman appears in more than one Amsterdam registration of intended marriage:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color
2 CONC : #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helve
2 CONC tica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;1. Jan Ammerman, from Moeri (probably Marien in East Frisia (Friesland, Germany), soldier, 29 years old, married on June 2, 1652 at Amstelveen with Annetje Roelofs, from Jever
2 CONC , 28 years old. (registration of intended marriage May 18, 1652, D.T.,B. 470/17)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #faf
2 CONC afa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica
2 CONC , arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;2. Gerrit Albert Ammerman, from Westerackum (Akkum lies in East Frisia, Germany), Tailor, 24 years old with Lucia Alderts, from Herver (Westerherver lies in Schleswig-Holstein, Ge
2 CONC rmany), 28 years old. (registration of intended marriage Amsterdam 1671, D.T.B. 497/269)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-col
2 CONC or: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', hel
2 CONC vetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;3. Jurjen Ammerman, from Wapelersijl (Wapelersiel, East Frisia (Oldenburg, Wiedersachsen), shoemaker, 28 years old, assisted by his uncle Dirck Teunisz with Zybrighje Eylder
2 CONC ts, from Amsterdam, 36 years old, assisted by her mother Jannetje Lubberts. (registration of intended marriage Amsterdam, October 1, 1678 D.T.B. 691/158)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pr
2 CONC o', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&l
2 CONC t;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;4. Roelf Ammerman,m from Jever (East Friesland, Niedersachsen, Germany), blacksmith, 26 years old with Ann
2 CONC a Jans (Jehnissen), from Jever, 29 years old. (registration of intended marriage Amsterdam, January 18, 1687 D.T.B. 659/31)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-ser
2 CONC if; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d
2 CONC ; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;It is probable that those bearing the name Ammerman that appear in Amsterdam, originally came from Ammerland (Oldenberg, Niedersachsen
2 CONC , Germany).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-f
2 CONC amily: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;Mu
2 CONC nicipal Archives Amsterdam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color
2 CONC : #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color
2 CONC : #fafafa;"&gt;D(oop), T(rouw) &amp;amp; B(egraafregisters) No. 466 p. 71 August 20, 1648&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-co
2 CONC lor: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', he
2 CONC lvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;Register of Intended marriage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15p
2 CONC x; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'sour
2 CONC ce sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;Appeared as above: registered on the deed of Nicolaas Cruquuis, minister at Ter Burght are Jacob Jansz Ammerman, sailor and Trijntie Claes, from Amsterdam
2 CONC , both living at Marcken.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #
2 CONC 36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #
2 CONC fafafa;"&gt;Remarks:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322
2 CONC d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafaf
2 CONC a;"&gt;Ter Burght is probably the town of Den Burg on the island Texel. I will try to find out if there was a reformed minister by the name of Nicolaas Cruquuis there. This registration on the basis of a deed probably points to this having been a h
2 CONC asty marriage. Perhaps because Jacob was due to sail. Perhaps Trijntie Claes sailed with him?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; backgroun
2 CONC d-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'source sans pro'
2 CONC , helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;"&gt;I don't know anything about the first generation of the Ammerman genealogy. The minister failed to give Jacob's place of birth. Both probably lived in Marken in Amsterd
2 CONC am, Marken was the name of an Amsterdam quarter but also the name of the tiny island in the Zuiderzee. I think that the name probably refers to the Amsterdam quarter here. They did not marry in Amsterdam, so that probably happened at Ter Burght (De
2 CONC n Burg on Texel).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
