1 _OID 3eb8972c-4c79-459a-8bbe-9646eb9843bd
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Paul, Abraham's second son, appears to have moved from the Esopus to Philipsburg Manor about twenty-five miles above New York City on the East side of the Hudson River.  There, on Oct. 10, 1708, he married Engeltje (Ange
2 CONC lica) Davidse, who had been born at Laval in Canada. They were married at the Dutch Reformed Church at Tarrytown, New York. They had five children. Engeltje died about 1716 and Paul married for the second time on Jan. 31, 1719, Elizabeth Foshier, d
2 CONC aughter of Jan and Eva. After their first child was born they moved to New Jersey, where they joined the Dutch Reformed Church at Hackensack.</line></content></metadataxml>
