1 _DSCR Watertown Re-Union
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;Mrs. Sarah Savage, relict of t h e late&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;Robert Savage,, died at her residence in&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;this place on Monday, March 1
2 CONC 5th, after&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;a long and painful illness, aged 75 years.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;Death has taken from us this time one of&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;our oldest and most r
2 CONC espected ladies. She&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;followed very quickly her husband, who&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;died only a year ago. She has been a&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;resident of this pl
2 CONC ace for the past forty&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;years. She had a fine memory and i t&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;was a r a r e treat to hear her tell of the&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;early settle
2 CONC ment of t h i s village. She has&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;been a p a t i e n t sufferer a long time and&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;waited patiently for t h e end, which she&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left
2 CONC "&gt;knew was near at hand. &amp;lt; She was a firm&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;believer in t h e Episcopal faith and will&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;be missed by all old and young,and i t will&lt;/p&gt;</line><line
2 CONC >&lt;p align="left"&gt;be a l o n g time before her name will be&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;forgotten, for she was a friend to a l l . Her&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;funeral was held at h e r late residence on&lt;/
2 CONC p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;Wednesday, March 17th, the Rev. Mr.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;Winnie officiating. She leaves three sons&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;to monrn her loss, Wm. Savage, of Yank&lt;
2 CONC /p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p align="left"&gt;ton, Dakota, Capt. James and George, of&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Dexter. They have t h e sympathy of all.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
