2 CONC t Crouse Irving Memorial Hospital. A native of Pittsburgh, Mrs. Sacco lived in the Syracuse area for 80 years. She retired after 21 years with General Electric Co. Mrs. Sacco was a communicant of St. Daniel's Church. Surviving are her husband, Fran
2 CONC k; a daughter, Sharon Updike of Liverpool; two sons, including Michael of Virginia; two sisters, Mary Harmon of Jamesville and Edith Zalanski of Syracuse; a brother, Joseph Galante of Cortland; five grandchildren; two great-grandchildren; and sever
2 CONC al nieces and nephews. Services will be at 8:30 a.m. Monday at Farone &amp;amp; Son Funeral Home and 9 a.m. in St. Daniel's Church. Burial will be in Woodlawn Mausoleum. Calling hours will be 2 to 4 and 7 to 9 p.m. today at the funeral home, 1500 P
