1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;Press and Sun-Bulletin (Binghamton, NY)&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;8 Sept. 1997&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Mrs. Theres
2 CONC a D. (Ted) (Chanecka) Kemp, 89, went to be with her Lord on Friday, September 5, 1997 at her home. She was predeceased by her husband Kenneth S. Kemp; two brothers, Paul and Joe Chanecka; and one grandson, Danny Kemp. She is survived by five sons a
2 CONC nd daughters-in-law, Kenneth S. and Charlene Kemp, Jr., Friendsville, Pa., Wayne H. and Elaine Kemp, Peekskill, NY., David P. and Yola Kemp, Binghamton, Donn B. and Jayne D. Kemp, Candor, Todd D. and Anne Kemp, Pleasantville, N.J.; 26 grandchildren
2 CONC ; 27 great grandchildren; three sisters and a brother-in-law, Julia and Marcel Hillis, Binghamton, Angeline Phillips, Binghamton, Mildred Chanecka, Deposit; two brothers and a sister-in-law, Steven Chanecka, Nanticoke, Pa., William and Agnes Chanec
2 CONC ka, Binghamton; and many nieces and nephews. Mrs. Kemp was a graduate of the Practical Bible College, Johnson City and a graduate of the Baptist Bible Seminary, Clark Summitt, Pa. She was a member of the Valleyview Alliance Church of Vestal and wa
2 CONC s also a Sunday school teacher and was involved in the shut-in ministry. She was also a member of the Endwell Garden Club.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Funeral services will be held Tuesday at 11 a.m. at t
2 CONC he Valleyview Alliance Church, 11 Foster Rd., Vestal. Rev. David M. Murphy, pastor of her church, will officiate. Burial will be in Riverhurst Cemetery, Endicott. The family will receive friends at the Allen Memorial Home, 511-513 E. Main St., Endi
2 CONC cott on Monday from 2 to 4 and 7 to 9 p.m. Expressions of sympathy in her memory may be made to the Missionary Fund c/o Valleyvire Alliance Church, 11 Foster Rd., Vestal, N.Y. 13850.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></conte
2 CONC nt></metadataxml>
