2 TITL Butler&#39;s Rangers
1 _OID 8ad856bc-9e1a-429b-8458-553165ebffcb
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.5em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: 'helvetica neue', helvetica, 'nimbus sans l', arial, 'liberation sans', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 26px; vertical-align: baseline; backg
2 CONC round-image: none; box-sizing: border-box; color: #252525; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);"&gt;&lt;strong style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant: inh
2 CONC erit; line-height: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box;"&gt;Butler's Rangers&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(1777&amp;ndash;1784) was a British provincial&amp;nbsp;regiment&amp;nbsp;composed of&amp;nbsp;Loyali
2 CONC sts&amp;nbsp;(or "Tories") in the&amp;nbsp;American Revolutionary War, raised by Loyalist&amp;nbsp;John Butler.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.5em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: 'helvetica neue', helvetica, 'nimbus sans l'
2 CONC , arial, 'liberation sans', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 26px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box; color: #252525; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);"&gt;Most members of the regiment we
2 CONC re Loyalists from&amp;nbsp;upstate New York. Among the regiment were former black slaves, the total number of black soldiers in Butler's Rangers is unknown, with estimates ranging from two to "more than a dozen". While some blacks served in&amp;nbs
2 CONC p;other units&amp;nbsp;and as&amp;nbsp;sappers&amp;nbsp;in the Engineer Corps and in the&amp;nbsp;Royal Artillery,&amp;nbsp;Sir William Howebanned the enlistment of blacks and ordered the disbanding of existing black regiments.&lt;sup style="margin
2 CONC : 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: inherit; font-size: 0.75em; font-style: inherit; font-variant: inherit; line-height: 1; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box;"&gt;&lt;span style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-
2 CONC family: inherit; font-size: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant: inherit; line-height: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box;"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p sty
2 CONC le="margin-: 0.5em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: 'helvetica neue', helvetica, 'nimbus sans l', arial, 'liberation sans', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 26px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border
2 CONC -box; color: #252525; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);"&gt;The Rangers were accused of participating in &amp;mdash; or at least failing to prevent &amp;mdash; the&amp;nbsp;Wyoming Valley massacre&amp;nbsp;of July 1778 and the&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ;Cherry Valley massacre&amp;nbsp;of November 1778 of white settlers (including some Loyalists) by&amp;nbsp;Joseph Brant's Iroquois. These actions earned the Rangers a reputation for exceptional savagery. They fought principally in&amp;nbsp;wester
2 CONC n New York&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;Pennsylvania, but ranged as far west as Ohio and Michigan and as far south as Virginia.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.5em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: 'helvetica neue', helvetica, 'nimbu
2 CONC s sans l', arial, 'liberation sans', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 26px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box; color: #252525; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);"&gt;Their winter quarter
2 CONC s were constructed on the west bank of the Niagara River in what is now the town of&amp;nbsp;Niagara-on-the-Lake, Ontario. Although the building that houses&amp;nbsp;&lt;em style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: inherit; font-s
2 CONC ize: inherit; font-variant: inherit; line-height: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box;"&gt;The&amp;nbsp;Lincoln and Welland Regiment&amp;nbsp;Museum&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;in that community is traditionall
2 CONC y known as "Butler's Barracks", it is not the original barracks and never housed Butler's Rangers. It was built in the years following the&amp;nbsp;War of 1812&amp;nbsp;to house the Indian department and received the name because Butler had bee
2 CONC n a Deputy Superintendent in that department.&lt;sup style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: inherit; font-size: 0.75em; font-style: inherit; font-variant: inherit; line-height: 1; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box;
2 CONC "&gt;&lt;span style="margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant: inherit; line-height: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box;"&gt;&
2 CONC lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
