1 DATE JANUARY 14, 1927
1 PLAC Watertown Daily Times
1 _DSCR Watertown Daily Times obit
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Gouverneur. Jan 24 &amp;mdash;Mrs. Esther &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Savage Mack. 82. died at tbe ho
2 CONC me &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;of her sister. &lt;strong&gt;&lt;font color="#ff0000"&gt;Mrs. Edward C. Sloat [mariah savage]. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Natural Dam. this morning at 1. She &lt;/font&gt;&lt;f
2 CONC ont size="3"&gt;was born in Dexter, Oct. 9. 1844. a &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;daughter of Thomas Savage, a native&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;of Ireland, and Marie Fife Savage, a &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;native of Scotland. &l
2 CONC t;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Fifty years ago Mrs. Mack was &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;married to Captain Martin Mack, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;known lake captain, of Water&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font f
2 CONC ace="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;town, who died in 1893. After their&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;marriage the couple resided for &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;some time in Watertown. A few &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;yea
2 CONC rs following the death of Captain &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Mack, his widow removed to &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Natural Dam where she had since &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;resided with her sister, Mrs. Sloat. .&lt;/font&gt;&l
2 CONC t;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Mrs. Mack leaves surviving be&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;sides her sister. Mrs. Sloat, tw
2 CONC o &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;nephews and one niece. She was a &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;member of the Episcopal church.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt; &lt;
2 CONC font size="3"&gt;Funeral services will be held Wednesday &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;morning at 10:30 from the home of her sister in Natural Dam. The body will be placed on the noon train to Watertown. &lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="1"
2 CONC &gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="1"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Burial will be in North Watertown Cemetery,&amp;nbsp; Rev V.O Boyle rector of t
2 CONC he Episcopal Church Governour &lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;and Rev. P. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;D.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&
2 CONC lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;Mang, pastor of the Methodist Episcopal Church at Natural Dam will officiate.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&
