2 TITL Contents of Johannes Adam Papst&#39;s Will
1 _OID a7e69235-5a27-4b16-a2c5-580b5dffd63c
1 _DSCR Contents of will
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;Source: &amp;nbsp;http://www.ffish.com/family_tree/Ancestors_Lorna/A1.htm#i1304&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;quo
2 CONC t;Transcription of Last Will &amp;amp; Testament of Adam Papst of Osnabruck, from a scanned image of the original, found on the internet. This transcription may contain errors:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The Last Will &a
2 CONC mp;amp; Testament of Adam Papst of Osnabruck&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Probate Granted 7th January 1819&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Entered in Book B-Pages 182 &amp;amp; 183&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;A McLean&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Reg S. C. E. D.&lt;/d
2 CONC iv&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;I Adam Papst of the Township of Osnabruck in the County of Stormont and Eastern district of the Province of Upper Canada Yeoman do make this my last Will and Testament in manner following, that is t
2 CONC o say I give devise and bequeath unto my Son John Papst all and every my real and personal Estate and Effects - whatsoever and wheresoever which I shall or may be possessed of or in anyways entitled unto at the time of my decease To hold to him hi
2 CONC s Heirs and Assigns, absolutely for ever Subject as follows. In the first place to the payment of all my just debts which I may happen to owe at the time of my decease and my funeral Expenses and the Expense of proving this my Will and all other Ch
2 CONC arges relating to the Execution thereof Also subject to the payment of fifty Dollars to Eve Mary Papst my Wife as soon after my Decease as the same can be Collected out of the hand of John Fetterley Junior and Adam Fetterley provided I shall not gi
2 CONC ve unto her hands the said Sum in my lifetime to be at her own disposal and for her &amp;lt;own&amp;gt; sSole use. Also subject to the Support and maintenance of the said Eve Mary Papst my wife in a Comfortable manner during her life provided she s
2 CONC hall reside with my said Son John&amp;#39;e Papst. But in Case the said Eve Mary Papst shall not find it Comfortable to live with my said Son then it is my Will that my said Son shall give unto her twelve Bushels of good and a Hog weighing one hund
2 CONC red and fifty pounds and ten dozen of Eggs yearly and every year during her natural life. Also my said Son shall give to the said Eve Mary Papst two good Cows at the time she chooses to depart from him for her better support. And my said Son shal
2 CONC l give to the said Eve Mary Papst six pounds of good wool yearly and every year from the time of my decease for her own Sole use and benefit whether she shall reside with him or not and permit her to enjoy and dispose of such goods and furniture a
2 CONC s are now her own Sole and Seperate property. And in Case the said Eve Mary Papst shall at any time be sick my siad Son shall procure her Medical assistance and proper nourishment and a fit woman to attend her during her indisposition whether she s
2 CONC hall live with my siad Son or not. And in Case of death my said Son shall cause her to be decently buried And it is my will that in Case my said Son John Papst shall dispose of the farm on which I now live in the life time of my said Wife Eve Mar
2 CONC y Papst, then my said Son shall pay or Secure to be paid to the said Eve Mary Papst her Heirs or Assigns one third part of the Value or Price the said farm shall be Sold for which Sum my said Wife shall have at her Sole disposal And I do hereby Con
2 CONC stitute and appoint John Loucks and Peter Darlington both of Osnabruck to be Executors of this my Will. And I do hereby revoke all former Wills by me made and declare this to be my last Will and Testament. In Witness whereof I have hereunto set m
2 CONC y hand and Seal this thirty first day of July in the Year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and three&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Adam Babst&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Signed Sealed publis
2 CONC hed and declared by the said Testator Adam Papst for his last Will and Testament in the presence of us who at his request and in his presence and in the presence of each other have hereunto Subscribed our Names as Witnesses thereto&lt;/div&gt;&lt;d
2 CONC iv&gt;Georg T Coons&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;George Wereley&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Peter Wereley&amp;quot;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
