1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;From EARLY FAMILIES OF HERKIMER COUNTY, NY, DESCENDANTS OF THE BURNETSFIELD PALATINES &amp;nbsp;BY WILLIAM V.H. BARKER:&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;861: &amp;nbsp;Lt. Col. Frederick PH Be
2 CONC llinger, &amp;nbsp;born 1727 (son of Philip); living May 1781 but died before 1783; married Catherine Weaver daughter of Nicholas Weaver. &amp;nbsp;Apparently in 1769 he was the Frederick P. Bellinger, clerk of Capt. Petrie's GF militia unit and du
2 CONC ring the Revolution became a high ranking officer serving in the 4th Tryon Co. Regiment. &amp;nbsp;He became a prisoner of war in 1777 and was listed as age 50 when parolled in Canada by Gen, Haldimand. &amp;nbsp;His parentage as son of Philip wa
2 CONC s established in a land transaction of his son Christopher (see Herkimer Co Deed Book 28 page 478 and E&amp;amp;N article of 20 Nov 1929 "Byt heir deeds shall ye know them"). &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
2 CONC </line></content></metadataxml>
