2 TITL Old South Cemetery Massachusetts (1)
1 _OID b1ebbf10-8087-43b3-871f-16cfba1d9158
1 _DSCR South Main Street
2 CONT Sherborn
2 CONT Middlesex County
2 CONT Massachusetts  USA
2 CONT Postal Code: 01770
2 CONT Phone: 508-651-7853
2 CONT http://www.sherbornma.org/page...
2 CONT 
2 CONT Cemetery notes and/or description:
2 CONT Old South Cemetery is Sherborn's most ancient burying ground. There is about it the same quiet simplicity that must have been present when Hopestill Leland was the first person buried here in 1655. Facing the walled entrance and backed by whisperin
2 CONC g pines is the Memorial Boulder inscribed on its inset bronze plaque, "The Most Ancient Burying Ground, On the West bank of the Charles River, Established by the Settlers of the Boggestowe Farms before 1660. Here rest from their labors The Founder
2 CONC s of Sherborn, Holliston, Medway. Erected by the Historical Societies of The Three Towns, 1915." Headstones were often not placed on graves in the early years of the settlement to keep the knowledge of their losses from the Indians. This fact, th
2 CONC e ravages of time and other circumstances result in there not being many of the earliest stones extant here, but there are several of the 'Memorable Mortality' of 1754.
