2 CONC , at the age of 72. A Pawleys Plantation resident, Michael was born in Syracuse, New York on September 6, 1946. Michael is survived by his loving wife, Carol Brown Sacco of Pawleys Island; his sister, Sharon Sacco of Syracuse, NY; nephew, Todd Paik
2 CONC in (Stacey) of Fort Lauderdale, FL; niece, Susan Hoalcraft of Syracuse, NY; brothers-in-law, Larry Brown (Alice) of Charlottesville, VA; and Alan Brown (Tina) of Pawleys Island.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Michael attended the University of Iow
2 CONC a on a football scholarship and completed graduate work at the University of Virginia. A retired Lt. Commander in the U.S. Navy, Michael valued his service to his country and continued to feel a strong connection with his military brethren. After m
2 CONC ilitary service, Michael worked as a sales representative for various organizations; served as President of the Black Hills Gold Company in Rapid City, SD; and represented Color Craft, a gemstone jewelry company in New York City.&lt;/p&gt;</line><l
2 CONC ine>&lt;p&gt;In selecting an area to live his retirement years, a prerequisite was a climate that allowed him to indulge in golfing on a regular basis, thus &amp;ndash; Pawleys Island. Never one to sit on the sidelines, Mike was formerly a member o
2 CONC f the Board of Visitors at the University of Virginia, and a member of Latrobe Country Club in Latrobe, PA. Currently, Mike belonged to the Wachesaw Plantation Club, was president of Wood Stork Landing HOA, served as a volunteer for the First Tee o
2 CONC f the Grand Strand, and was a member of Precious Blood of Christ Catholic Church. While no longer able to sit in the bleachers as a season pass holder, Mike will continue to cheer on the Coastal Carolina Chanticleers from above.&lt;/p&gt;</line><li
2 CONC ne>&lt;p&gt;A funeral service will be held at 11:00 am Monday, December 24, 2018, at Precious Blood of Christ Catholic Church. Burial will follow at Pawleys Island Presbyterian Church Cemetery.&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/
2 CONC span&gt;The family will receive friends from 2:00 &amp;ndash; 6:00 pm Sunday, December 23, 2018, at Goldfinch Funeral Home, Litchfield/Pawleys Chapel.&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;I
2 CONC n lieu of flowers, memorial contributions may be made in the name of Michael Sacco to Father Pat&amp;rsquo;s Kitchen, 1633 Waverly Road, Pawleys Island, SC 29585; or to Disabled Veterans, DAV Chapter 30, PO Box 30637, Myrtle Beach, SC 29588.&lt;/p&
2 CONC gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Sign an online guestbook at &lt;span&gt;www.goldfinchfuneralhome.com&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Goldfinch Funeral Home, Beach Chapel is in charge of the arrangements.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;!--
2 CONC EndFragment--&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
