1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&amp;nbsp;</line><line>&amp;nbsp;</line><line>&lt;p style="border: 0px; margin-: 0.4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; caret-color: #3a3a3a; color: #3a3a3a; font-family: 'helvetica neue', h
2 CONC elvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000000; font-family: verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;1636 Dedham Compact&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="border: 0px; margin-: 0
2 CONC .4em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; caret-color: #3a3a3a; color: #3a3a3a; font-family: 'helvetica neue', helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;He was one of the signa
2 CONC tories to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style="font-size: 14px; border: 0px; font-style: inherit; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;Dedham Compact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;, a key historical d
2 CONC ocument for the creation of the new colonial town of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Dedham, Massachusetts&lt;span style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;, located in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;&am
2 CONC p;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Norfolk County, Massachusetts&lt;span style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;. The first 35 signatures were collected in August 1636 and another 90 more soon thereafter. This document provided for the common governance and defense of the c
