2 CONC . Some historians say that she married John Penticost after Edward's death, but this is not correct. John Penticot married a Joanna Larkin in 1639, two years after Edward &amp;amp; Joanna (Butler) Larkin were married. The Joanna Larkin that John Pe
2 CONC nticost married was probably Edward's sister.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She was admitted to the church in Charlestown on January 8, 1638/39. After Edward's death in 1652, widow Joanna Larkin was granted 12 acres of woodland &amp;amp; 2 acres of common o
2 CONC n the mystic side as part of the widow's dower on March 1, 1658.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Family links: &lt;br&gt;Spouse:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a class="NoUnderline12point" href="fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;amp;GRid=32696054"&gt;Edward Larkin (1603 - 1
