2 CONC &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 12px; white-space: nowrap;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;Loyalist leader Sir John Johnson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span sty
2 CONC le="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;from American refugees fleeing rebel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium; line-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;persecution,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="f
2 CONC ont-size: 8px; line-height: 7px; white-space: nowrap;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium; line-height: 26px;"&gt;the regiment served with distinction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 8px; line-height: 7px; white-spac
2 CONC e: nowrap;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;throughout the war, launching raids and relief missions into the Mohawk Valley&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: m
2 CONC edium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;of New York.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.5em; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: 'helvetica neue', helvetica, 'nimbus sans l', arial, 'libe
2 CONC ration sans', sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box; color: #252525; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 26px;"&gt;As one of the most active
2 CONC &amp;nbsp;Loyalist regiments in the Canadian department, it was instrumental in the siege of&amp;nbsp;Fort Stanwix&amp;nbsp;during the expedition of Colonel&amp;nbsp;St. Leger&amp;nbsp;down the&amp;nbsp;Mohawk River Valley&amp;nbsp;in the summer o
2 CONC f 1777.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12px; line-height: 12px; white-space: nowrap;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;The regiment saw action at the Battle of Oriskany&
2 CONC lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;in 1777,&amp;nbsp;Carleton's Raid (1778)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 2
2 CONC 6px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;and the devastating raid on the Schoharie Valley&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;in 1780. Along with American Indain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;sp
2 CONC an style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;allies and fellow provincial regiments such as&amp;nbsp;Butler's Rangers,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height
2 CONC : 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;the regiment fought a series of low-level raiding campaigns through the Mohawk Valley. This region was a major agricultural area of New York, and these raids were intended to interdict the supply of foodstuffs to General Georg
2 CONC e Washington's&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;army while pressuring the Revolution's&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="l
2 CONC ine-height: 26px;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;political leaders in the region, who were actively persecuting loyalist residents as traitors aiding and supplying British troops.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;sup style="font-size: 0.75em; line-height: 1; margin: 0p
2 CONC x; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant: inherit; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box; white-space: nowrap;"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0.5em; paddi
2 CONC ng: 0px; border: 0px; font-family: 'helvetica neue', helvetica, 'nimbus sans l', arial, 'liberation sans', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 26px; vertical-align: baseline; background-image: none; box-sizing: border-box; color: #252525; -we
2 CONC bkit-tap-highlight-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);"&gt;The regiment eventually comprised two battalions. Following the war, the first battalion was disbanded in 1783 and the second battalion in 1784. Members of the regiment were granted land along the&amp
2 CONC ;nbsp;St. Lawrence River&amp;nbsp;valley and&amp;nbsp;Bay of Quintein modern Ontario and were among the first settlers of&amp;nbsp;Upper Canada, later the province of&amp;nbsp;Ontario&amp;nbsp;in&amp;nbsp;Canada.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadat
