1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;1. Thomas Rider, son of William, 3d, and Elizabeth (Hill Rider, was b. in Natick, Mass., June 28, 1761.&amp;nbsp; The place and date of his death have not been discovered by us.&amp;nbsp; He came from Natick t
2 CONC o Sullivan, in 1798, and purchased of Thomas Beals the farm where Lucius Nims and Hon. D.W. Rugg have lived in later years. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;His house at 21, partly covering the site of Mr. Rugg&amp;#39;s house, but, according to his niece, the l
2 CONC ate Miss Martha (or Patty)Leland, it projected a few feet farther to the south than the present house.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He married Dec. 18, 1783, in Natick, Mass., Anne Haven, B. in Natick, July 31, 1766; daughter of David and Abigail (Prentiss) H
2 CONC aven.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have not learned the place and date of her death.&amp;nbsp; Mr. Rider was a good farmer.&amp;nbsp; He had nine children.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1. Sarah (Sally) Rider, born in Natick, Mass., May 26, 1784; married James Wilso
2 CONC n (q.v. in the Daniel Wilson Family).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. Isaac Rider, born in Natick,Mass., March 10, 1787; married in 1810, Abigail Mason of Dublin (born there APril 4, 1783; daughter of Benjamin, Jr. and Phebe (Norcross)Mason. They lived at Ler
2 CONC oy, N.Y., where Abigail died, leaving one child.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. Betsey Rider, born in Natick, Mass., Sept. 25, 1791; Married Asa Mason, q.v.; removed to Leroy New York.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;4. Abigail (Nabby) Rider, born in Natick, Mass.,Aug. 26
2 CONC , 1794; no more learned respecting her.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;5. Hannah Rider, born in Natick, Mass., Aug. 31, 1797; died there, Oct. 14, 1797.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;6. Calvin Rider, born in Sullivan, at 21(address?), Feb. 20, 1799, moved out of the state
2 CONC , when young, with his parents.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;7. Luther Rider, born in Sullivan, at 21(address?), March 20, 1802, moved, when young with his parents to another state.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;8. Walter Sawyer Rider, born in Sullivan, at 21 (address?),
2 CONC Oct. 13, 1806, moved from state, in infancy, with his parents.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;9. William Rider, born Nov. 12, 1809, in Leroy, New York, where all of the family of Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Rider and their married children are said to have moved. &lt;/
2 CONC p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
