1 _OID d1f4c629-09ca-4011-8fdf-c8a016bf6fca
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;pre&gt;A professional soldier, Peter was with the Scotch Greys and Dragoons under Wellington when Napoleon was defeated at Waterloo. He also served with the Imperial Army in </line><line>India before settling in Cana
2 CONC da in 1831. For sometime he was lockmaster at Black Rapids on the Rideau River and acquired property (presumably by Crown Lands Grant) </line><line>at what is now the corner of Parkdale Avenue and Carling Avenue. For a time his daughter Jessica liv
2 CONC ed with the Black family on the 10th Concession of Goulbourn </line><line>(now called Fernbank Road) but when she needed medical care she became one of the early patients at the Perley Home in Ottawa, where she died about 1910. &lt;/pre&gt;</line><
2 CONC /content></metadataxml>
