2 CONC h in </line><line>Brookheld. delivered an historical discourse, in which he gave an account of the settlement ot </line><line>the town and its distresses during the Indian wars. The principal portions of this address&amp;mdash; </line><line>which w
2 CONC as published by Thomas and John Fleet, Boston. 1776&amp;mdash; were printed in the Col- </line><line>lections of the Massachusetts Historical Society, I.. 1792. The opening pages of this, cover- </line><line>ing the early history of the town up t
