1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;Coroner's Inquest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt
2 CONC ;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;FOUND IN A FIELD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p
2 CONC &gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;The Suspicious Death of Moses Black&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<
2 CONC /line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;CORNER'S INQUEST</line><line>&lt;/span&gt;
2 CONC &lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;AN OPEN VERDICT RETURNED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'courier new'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Corner Corbett ye
2 CONC sterday held an inquest on the body of Moses Black, who was found dead in a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;field at Stittsville, as announced by telegraph in yesterday'
2 CONC s Free Press. The</line><line>inquest was held at the residence of the deceased, in the township of</line><line>Goulbourn, some five miles distant from where the body was found.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size
2 CONC : 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;The evidence given throws but little light upon the cause of Black's death. It was known
2 CONC </line><line>that he left home on Friday last, with the avowed purpose of going to Richmond Village</line><line>for some letters which he said he expected with remittances. At this time he</line><line>was not known to have any money, and intended
2 CONC , if he obtained the expected remittance,</line><line>visiting his daughter at Luther, Ont. He was seen in Richmond the same day and</line><line>rode a portion of the way home with Ellen Shannon and her son. He had with him</line><line>a tea pot, s
2 CONC ome bread and a couple of walking canes. He got off near the residence</line><line>of John Forbes, not far from which the body was found. The body was discovered</line><line>in the Forbes field, about five o'clock on Monday evening. There was a cu
2 CONC t on</line><line>the forehead, the arms were bruised and the coat torn. At his feet were two letters,</line><line>one of which had evidently been in his pocket for sometime, and one from his</line><line>daughter, which it is supposed he obtained fr
2 CONC om the post office at Richmond when</line><line>last there. The deceased who was almost fifty (85?) years of age, has several &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;married chil
2 CONC dren. No post mortem was held, as it was impossible to secure the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;attendance of a medical man. The jury returned an open verdict. It is pr
2 CONC obable that some further</line><line>investigation will be held and the matter thoroughly sifted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><
2 CONC line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;EVIDENCE AT INQUEST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;The jury empanelled consisted of James S
2 CONC hannon, foreman; William Alexander, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;John Shannon, George Keyes, Thomas Devine, Edward Shannon, Alexander Graham, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</
2 CONC line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;Henry Cooper, James Porteous, James Graham, Patrick McPherson, James McKirby and George</line><line>Graham. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span s
2 CONC tyle="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;James Shannon was the first witness. He stated that he saw the body of th
2 CONC e &lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'courier new'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;deceased in Forbes' field; the clothes were torn and there was a large wound on the right&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-siz
2 CONC e: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;side of the head, and also bruises and marks on the arms; the body was in a</line><line>sitting posture against the fence, one hand being against the stomach; knew the</line><line>remains to be those of Mose
2 CONC s Black; John Devine and James Fitzgerald were with</line><line>him at the time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt
2 CONC ;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;James Porteous, grandson of the deceased, testified that he was present when the body was found</line><line>in Forbes' Field; saw a large mark above the eye and one on the right arm; the
2 CONC </line><line>deceased's coat was badly torn; John Black took two letters off the body and he</line><line>(witness) took the money ($7.85?), afterwards gave the money to John Black to</line><line>go to Richmond Village to get a coffin. &lt;/span&gt;
2 CONC &lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'courier new'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Ellen Shannon stated that she was at Richmond on Friday last, overtook him on the road and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="
2 CONC font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;gave him a lift in their wagon; left him at Mr. Forbes' gate 8th line in Goulbourn;</line><line>deceased was then in good health and seemed to be alright; he had several packages</line><line>with him
2 CONC , one containing a loaf of bread, also a teapot and two walking sticks,</line><line>which he used in walking.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p
2 CONC &gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;John Forbes testified that the deceased had tea at his place on the evening of Friday, August</line><line>19th; that yesterday (Monday) evening about five o'
2 CONC clock his boy called him and</line><line>said that they had found a man asleep or dead in the fields, on going to the</line><line>place saw deceased dead, sitting against the fence; the deceased's clothes were</line><line>torn and there was a larg
2 CONC e mark on his right forehead; did not recognize it as</line><line>Black's body at first - the witness went to a Magistrate, and was told to go to</line><line>Dr. Beatty at Richmond, and telegraph Dr. Coroner Corbett at Ottawa and did so.&lt;/span&g
2 CONC t;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;This was all the evidence taken, and the jury returned an open verdict, Dr. Corbett considers</line><line>the death a very suspicious one, and worth
2 CONC y of further investigation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'courier new';"&gt;Of the two letters one was an old one, and had been registered. The other was a late one</line><line>from his d
2 CONC aughter, dated Luther July 18, 1881. It was a kind invitation for the</line><line>old man to come up and live with her and her sister. The deceased was living in</line><line>a house on his children's place in Goulbourn.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line
