1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;SMETHPORT - Kathleen Norma Greene, 86, of Smethport, formerly of East Valley Rd., died Monday (Dec. 17, 2012) in the Bradford Regional Medical Center, Bradford.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She was born Feb 26, 1926, in B
2 CONC uffalo, a daughter of George and Katherine Hupf Brodfuehrer. On July 6, 1946, in Buffalo, she married Wallace Watson Greene, who died Nov. 30, 1998.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mrs. Greene worked in the Cafeteria of the Smethport Area High School for many y
2 CONC ears and retired in 1998.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She was a member of Smethport Senior Center and St. Elizabeth of Hungary Church, Smethport.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She is survived by three daughters, Elizabeth G. Sweet, Rose Marie Jackson and Theresa Ann R
2 CONC obinson; four sons, David W. Greene, Larry A. Greene, Thomas S. Greene and Raymond E. Greene; 19 grandchildren; 24 great-grandchildren; a sister, Mary Cooper; and several nieces and nephews.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition to her parents and husband
2 CONC , she was preceded in death by a son, John Patrick Greene; a daughter, Karen Ann Schneider; seven brothers; and one sister.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Visitation will be held on Wednesday from 2-4 and 6-8 p.m. at Hartle-Tarbox Funeral Homes, Inc., 2 Bank S
2 CONC t., Smethport, Pa., where funeral and committal services will be held on Thursday, Dec. 20 at 11 a.m., with the Rev. Vincent P. Cieslewicz, pastor of St. Elizabeth Church, Smethport, officiating. Burial will be in St. Elizabeth Cemetery, Smethport
2 CONC . A Christian Wake service will be held at 3:30 p.m. Wednesday afternoon.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
