2 TITL The Tale of Two Girls named Anna Kuhn
1 _OID e43d9e3d-818c-45f7-b603-532b75b72a16
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="white-space: pre"&gt;	&lt;/span&gt;It isn&amp;#39;t as if searching for your family history isn&amp;#39;t hard enough, do we really have to confuse things further with sisters named Anna Kuhn. T
2 CONC o top that off, they married two men named Bellinger.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anna Kuhn (birth date ?)- daughter of Hans Kuhn - Married Jorge Bruning b abt 1660- widowed- married 2nd Nicholas Bellinger (his 2nd wife) 25 Nov 1685. Could her middle name b
2 CONC e Marie. I found an Anna Marie Kuhn born in 1661. Could they be twins? We may never know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anna Margaretha Kuhn (1661-1725)- daughter of Hans Kuhn- Married to Johannes Frederich Bellinger (1664-1725) in 1690.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I fo
2 CONC und info on both Anna&amp;#39;s in a book called &amp;quot;Early Families of Herkimer County, New York&amp;quot;. It is on the internet.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
