2 CONC ountryside": &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #181a1c; font-family: 'source sans pro', 'helvetica neue', arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; white-space: pre-wrap;"&gt;Margaret was "a rather petite woman but healt
2 CONC hy and active... She had a reputation as an especially competent midwife." "On occasional summer afternoons, even when she was well up in years, Granny would decide to visit one of her old friends in the vicinity. Dressed in her best blouse, full s
2 CONC kirt over layers of stiff petticoats, bonnet and shawl, and accompanied by one or two grandchildren, off she would go, grandly, in the buggy, holding the reins of a gentle driving horse. The roads were narrow gravelled ribbons, but there were no au
2 CONC tomobiles to compete with, and she made it a point, after a pleasant chat and the customary hospitality of tea and cake, to return before darkness fell. Granny had a great deal of energy for her age and when she was over seventy, she still sometime
2 CONC s skipped rope with the children. One day at the school this was mentioned, and the child was accused of boasting. whereupon the skeptics were invited to come home for first-hand proof. Although not eager to comply, with a little coaxing and in th
2 CONC e interest of the grandchildren's reputation, Granny gave a snappy demonstration with pepper skipping as a finale."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
